WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:15.663 --> 00:00:21.482
The pandemic has certainly increased
violence against people with disabilities

00:00:21.482 --> 00:00:28.593
because everyone was locked
in their house.

00:00:28.593 --> 00:00:36.952
And in these four walls,
very difficult situations took place, 

00:00:36.952 --> 00:00:43.973
which has been talked about
and noted in Poland.

00:00:44.603 --> 00:00:52.435
In addition, people with disabilities
are a group more exposed to Covid-19, 

00:00:52.435 --> 00:00:56.885
which has had a great impact
on their situation,

00:00:56.885 --> 00:00:59.827
on their ability to create,

00:00:59.827 --> 00:01:07.520
because being at home
doesn't help in creating.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:12.037
Myself, being locked in my apartment,

00:01:12.037 --> 00:01:20.757
my motivation dropped automatically
and I started to focus on my health.

00:01:20.757 --> 00:01:24.670
The fact that it is the most important thing.

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:27.638
And I think that many people
with disabilities 

00:01:27.638 --> 00:01:32.225
seem to have left
their careers behind

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:39.128
because their health situation
was more important.

00:01:40.323 --> 00:01:43.542
Maybe emotionally what I felt

00:01:43.542 --> 00:01:50.357
was to be even more fragile
as a disabled artist in general

00:01:50.357 --> 00:01:55.950
because sometimes I feel a bit insecure
and I think my insecurity comes from there.

00:01:56.152 --> 00:01:58.393
That affected me a lot.

00:01:58.393 --> 00:02:01.790
The contact with the people,

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:05.145
all the communications,

00:02:05.145 --> 00:02:10.750
all that has to do with culture,

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.918
to learn some things...

00:02:16.918 --> 00:02:20.153
I've noticed, since I don't have to travel,

00:02:20.153 --> 00:02:22.637
it kind of reduced stress for me

00:02:22.637 --> 00:02:26.883
like living in Berlin,
getting along,

00:02:26.883 --> 00:02:31.675
finding things,
having to take the subway every day,

00:02:31.675 --> 00:02:33.748
that reduced so much stress.

00:02:38.653 --> 00:02:41.275
I will speak from my experience
as a deaf person,

00:02:41.275 --> 00:02:43.343
Covid-19 gave me

00:02:45.125 --> 00:02:48.197
the opportunity to face

00:02:48.197 --> 00:02:50.835
which body I have.

00:02:50.835 --> 00:02:54.617
For example, when people are talking
about something

00:02:54.617 --> 00:02:57.238
and everybody has their masks on
and I'm like: 

00:02:57.238 --> 00:02:59.540
"Guys, would you like to share?"

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:03.755
The world is going faster than you
and it doesn't wait for you

00:03:03.755 --> 00:03:06.353
and I'm not asking the world
to wait for me,

00:03:06.353 --> 00:03:08.710
I'm just asking you to do
this simple movement.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:13.353
Covid-19 took off our bodies from the society,

00:03:13.353 --> 00:03:16.318
not just mine but even yours,
even able bodies,

00:03:16.318 --> 00:03:20.757
everybody's bodies were taken off
the society

00:03:20.757 --> 00:03:24.202
because we were at home,
locked down, etc.

00:03:24.202 --> 00:03:27.828
It was a moment in which I really
understood my body,

00:03:27.828 --> 00:03:30.280
this part of my body,

00:03:32.792 --> 00:03:36.887
and without that pride coming from
telling people I'm deaf

00:03:36.887 --> 00:03:39.630
I don't know which kind of art
I would have done.

